  <static seed="238" source="Library/272/setStewart13_2/problem_4.pg">
    <statement><p>Find parametric equations for line that is tangent to the curve <m>x=\cos t,\  y=\sin t, \ z=t</m> at the point</p>
<p><m>(\cos(\frac{-2\pi}{6}) ,\sin(\frac{-2\pi}{6}) ,\frac{-2\pi}{6} )</m> 
  .</p>
<p>Parametrize the line so that it passes through the given point at t=0.  All three answers are required for credit.</p>
<p><m>x(t)</m> = <fillin characters="40" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p><m>y(t)</m> = <fillin characters="40" name="MuLtIaNsWeR_AnSwEr0001_1"/></p>
<p><m>z(t)</m> = <fillin characters="40" name="MuLtIaNsWeR_AnSwEr0001_2"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\cos\mathopen{}\left(\frac{-2\pi }{6}\right)+-\sin\mathopen{}\left(\frac{-2\pi }{6}\right)t;\,\sin\mathopen{}\left(\frac{-2\pi }{6}\right)+\cos\mathopen{}\left(\frac{-2\pi }{6}\right)t;\,\frac{-2\pi }{6}+t</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
